IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `fca4a-dates`

-- Federal Court of Australia Act 1976 (Cth), Part IVA (representative proceedings, "class actions") and s 43(1A) --
-- the rules a group member, or a person who starts a class action, meets.
--
-- Based on content from the Federal Register of Legislation: "Federal Court of Australia Act 1976", Compilation No. 59
-- (compilation date 11 December 2024, register id C2024C00819), and "Federal Court Rules 2011", Compilation No. 11
-- (compilation date 11 June 2026, register id F2026C00512), Commonwealth of Australia, licensed under CC BY 4.0
-- (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Quotations are from the deposited plain-text conversions at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A01586.txt and ../../../federal-court-rules-2011/registers/source-bundle/F2011L01551.txt.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.
--
-- Negatives follow the rulings of 2026-11-04 and 2026-11-05 (docs/ENCODING-GUIDE.md section 5): JUST FALSE where the
-- text itself says no; NOTHING where it does not answer, each tagged "NOTHING-kind" with the reason. Where the Court
-- decides (it "may", it is "satisfied", it "thinks fit"), JUST TRUE means the Court can do it, never that it will; the
-- Court's judgments are taken as inputs.

§ `Federal Court of Australia Act 1976 -- Part IVA`

-- A MAYBE BOOLEAN conjunction: a no in either part is a no; otherwise an unanswered part leaves the whole unanswered.
GIVEN a IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN, b IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`both` a b MEANS
    IF (a EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (b EQUALS JUST FALSE)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF (a EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (b EQUALS JUST TRUE)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Division 1 and 2 -- who can bring a class action (ss 33B, 33C, 33D, 33G)`

-- s 33B: "A proceeding may only be brought under this Part in respect of a cause of action arising after the
-- commencement of the Federal Court of Australia Amendment Act 1991." The endnotes (Act No. 181, 1991) give its
-- commencement as 4 March 1992. An Act commences at the start of its day, so a cause of action arising on 4 March 1992
-- arose after it (fork F1).
`commencement of the Federal Court of Australia Amendment Act 1991` MEANS `the day` 4 3 1992

GIVEN `the day it arose` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 33B -- the cause of action arose after the 1991 commencement` `the day it arose` IF
    `days from` `commencement of the Federal Court of Australia Amendment Act 1991` `the day it arose` AT LEAST 0

-- s 33C(1) "where: (a) 7 or more persons have claims against the same person; and (b) the claims ... are in respect of,
-- or arise out of, the same, similar or related circumstances; and (c) the claims ... give rise to a substantial common
-- issue of law or fact; a proceeding may be commenced". s 33C(2): the kind of relief and separate contracts or acts make
-- no difference, so they are not asked. s 33G: "may not be commenced if" the Court's only jurisdiction is cross-vesting.
-- A failed "where", "only" or "may not" is the text's no (rulings (b), "only", flat negative).
GIVEN `the day it arose` IS A DATE, `how many claimants` IS A NUMBER, `same similar or related circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `substantial common issue` IS A BOOLEAN, `jurisdiction only by cross-vesting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33C -- the claims can be brought as a representative proceeding` `the day it arose` `how many claimants` `same similar or related circumstances` `substantial common issue` `jurisdiction only by cross-vesting` MEANS
    IF      `s 33B -- the cause of action arose after the 1991 commencement` `the day it arose`
        AND `how many claimants` AT LEAST 7
        AND `same similar or related circumstances`
        AND `substantial common issue`
        AND (NOT `jurisdiction only by cross-vesting`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 33D(1): a person within s 33C(1)(a) "who has a sufficient interest to commence a proceeding on his or her own behalf"
-- against the other person has a sufficient interest to commence the representative proceeding. Without that interest
-- the section is silent. NOTHING-kind: silent (the Act does not say who else lacks standing).
GIVEN `sufficient interest on my own behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33D(1) -- I have standing to commence` `sufficient interest on my own behalf` MEANS
    IF `sufficient interest on my own behalf`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 33D(2): "Where a person has commenced a representative proceeding, the person retains a sufficient interest: (a) to
-- continue that proceeding; and (b) to bring an appeal ... even though the person ceases to have a claim". "Where" not
-- met: JUST FALSE for this section (ruling (b)); the person may have an interest on some other footing (fork F2).
GIVEN `I commenced it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33D(2) -- I keep my standing without a claim` `I commenced it` MEANS
    IF `I commenced it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Who is a group member (ss 33A, 33E, 33F)`

-- s 33E(2) lists who must consent in writing (Federal Court Rules 2011 r 9.33: Form 20). Everyone else needs no consent
-- (s 33E(1)).
DECLARE `Kind of person` IS ONE OF
    `an individual or a company or other person not listed`
    `the Commonwealth or a State or a Territory`
    `a Minister of the Commonwealth or of a State or Territory`
    `a public-purpose body corporate that is not an incorporated company or association`
    `an officer of the Commonwealth or a State or Territory acting as such`

GIVEN k IS A `Kind of person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 33E(2) -- consent in writing is needed` k IF
    NOT (k EQUALS `an individual or a company or other person not listed`)

-- s 33A "group member means a member of a group of persons on whose behalf a representative proceeding has been
-- commenced" (a "means" definition; outside the group described, no). s 33E(2) "None of the following persons is a group
-- member ... unless the person gives written consent" (an "unless": without consent, no).
GIVEN `the group described includes me` IS A BOOLEAN, k IS A `Kind of person`, `I gave written consent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 33A, 33E -- I am a group member` `the group described includes me` k `I gave written consent` MEANS
    IF NOT `the group described includes me`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `s 33E(2) -- consent in writing is needed` k AND (NOT `I gave written consent`)
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `What I want to do` IS ONE OF
    `be a group member`
    `take a step in the proceeding or conduct part of it`

-- s 33F(1) "It is not necessary for a person under disability to have a next friend or committee merely in order to be a
-- group member." (2) such a member "may only take a step ... by his or her next friend or committee". For a person not
-- under disability the section says nothing. NOTHING-kind: scope limit (the section speaks only of persons under
-- disability).
GIVEN `I am under disability` IS A BOOLEAN, w IS A `What I want to do`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33F -- I need a next friend or committee` `I am under disability` w MEANS
    IF NOT `I am under disability`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER w
         WHEN `be a group member` THEN JUST FALSE
         WHEN `take a step in the proceeding or conduct part of it` THEN JUST TRUE

§§ `Opting out (ss 33J, 33ZC(8))`

-- s 33J(1) the Court fixes a date; (3) it may fix another date to extend the period; (2) "A group member may opt out ...
-- by written notice given under the Rules of Court before the date so fixed." r 9.34: "An opt out notice under section
-- 33J(2) of the Act must be in accordance with Form 21." s 33ZC(8): "Section 33J does not apply to an appeal proceeding."
-- "before the date": the fixed date itself is too late (finding 1). The period is the text's own (ruling (a)): outside it,
-- JUST FALSE. A notice not in writing in Form 21 falls outside the grant's own wording: NOTHING (fork F3).
GIVEN `the opt-out date` IS A DATE, `the day I give notice` IS A DATE, `written notice in Form 21` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `this is an appeal proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33J(2) -- I can opt out` `the opt-out date` `the day I give notice` `written notice in Form 21` `this is an appeal proceeding` MEANS
    IF `this is an appeal proceeding`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `days from` `the day I give notice` `the opt-out date` AT MOST 0
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF `written notice in Form 21`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING

GIVEN `the opt-out date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 33J(2) -- the last day to opt out` `the opt-out date` MEANS
    `the day n days after` `the opt-out date` (0 MINUS 1)

-- s 33J(4) "Except with the leave of the Court, the hearing ... must not commence earlier than the date before which a
-- group member may opt out". A flat negative: earlier than that date and without leave, no.
GIVEN `the hearing day` IS A DATE, `the opt-out date` IS A DATE, `the Court gave leave` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33J(4) -- the hearing can start then` `the hearing day` `the opt-out date` `the Court gave leave` MEANS
    IF `days from` `the opt-out date` `the hearing day` AT LEAST 0
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `the Court gave leave`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Later claims (s 33K)`

-- s 33K(1), (2): on the representative party's application the Court may give leave to alter the group "so as to include
-- a person: (a) whose cause of action accrued after the commencement ... but before such date as the Court fixes when
-- giving leave; and (b) who would have been included ... if the cause of action had accrued before the commencement".
-- Outside (a) or (b) the grant's own wording does not reach the person. NOTHING-kind: limit of a grant's wording (an
-- earlier claim belongs in the original description; fork F4).
GIVEN `the day my cause accrued` IS A DATE, `the day the class action began` IS A DATE, `the date the Court fixes` IS A DATE,
      `I would have been included` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33K -- the group can be altered to include me` `the day my cause accrued` `the day the class action began` `the date the Court fixes` `I would have been included` MEANS
    IF      `days from` `the day the class action began` `the day my cause accrued` GREATER THAN 0
        AND `days from` `the day my cause accrued` `the date the Court fixes` GREATER THAN 0
        AND `I would have been included`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `When it stops being a class action (ss 33L, 33M, 33N, 33P)`

-- s 33L "If ... it appears likely to the Court that there are fewer than 7 group members"; s 33M "Where: (a) the relief
-- ... is or includes payment of money to group members ... and (b) on application by the respondent, the Court concludes
-- that ... the cost ... of identifying the group members and distributing ... would be excessive"; s 33N(1) "where it is
-- satisfied that it is in the interests of justice to do so because" one of (a)-(d). Each is an "if" or "where": none
-- met, no order under these sections. s 33ZG(b) keeps the Court's other powers (abuse of process and the like), which
-- are not answered here.
GIVEN `group members the Court thinks likely` IS A NUMBER, `money is claimed for group members` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Court concludes distribution would cost too much` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Court is satisfied under s 33N` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 33L, 33M, 33N -- the Court can stop the class action` `group members the Court thinks likely` `money is claimed for group members` `the Court concludes distribution would cost too much` `the Court is satisfied under s 33N` MEANS
    IF     `group members the Court thinks likely` LESS THAN 7
        OR (`money is claimed for group members` AND `the Court concludes distribution would cost too much`)
        OR `the Court is satisfied under s 33N`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 33P "Where the Court makes an order under section 33L, 33M or 33N that a proceeding no longer continue under this
-- Part: (a) the proceeding may be continued ... by the representative party on his or her own behalf ...; and (b) on the
-- application of a person who was a group member ..., the Court may order that the person be joined as an applicant".
-- No such order: the "where" fails (JUST FALSE).
-- (a) is for the representative party, (b) for a group member on application; either way the answer is the same.
GIVEN `the Court ordered it no longer continue` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33P -- I can go on with my own claim in it` `the Court ordered it no longer continue` MEANS
    IF `the Court ordered it no longer continue`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Costs (s 43(1A), ss 33Q(3), 33R(2))`

DECLARE `My part in the class action` IS ONE OF
    `a group member who is not a party`
    `a group member allowed to appear on an issue about my own claim`
    `a sub-group representative party who is not the representative party`
    `the representative party`

DECLARE `Kind of costs` IS ONE OF
    `costs of the proceeding generally`
    `costs of the issues common to my sub-group`
    `costs of an issue about one member's claim only`

-- s 43(1A): in a Part IVA proceeding the Court "may not award costs against a person on whose behalf the proceeding has
-- been commenced (other than a party to the proceeding who is representing such a person) except as authorised by ...
-- section 33Q or 33R". s 33Q(3): a sub-group representative party who is not the representative party, "and not the
-- representative party, is liable for costs associated with the determination of the issue or issues common to the
-- sub-group members". s 33R(2): the individual group member allowed to appear, "and not the representative party, is
-- liable for costs associated with the determination of the issue". A party who represents others is under the Court's
-- general power in s 43(1) and (2). JUST TRUE means the Court can order it.
GIVEN p IS A `My part in the class action`, c IS A `Kind of costs`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 43(1A) -- costs can be awarded against me` p c MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `a group member who is not a party` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `a group member allowed to appear on an issue about my own claim` THEN
        CONSIDER c
        WHEN `costs of an issue about one member's claim only` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
    WHEN `a sub-group representative party who is not the representative party` THEN
        CONSIDER c
        WHEN `costs of the issues common to my sub-group` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind: silent. The sub-group representative is a party representing others, so s 43(1A) does not shield
        -- them, but neither s 33Q(3) nor s 43 says whether they bear the group's general costs or another member's (fork F5).
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
    WHEN `the representative party` THEN
        CONSIDER c
        WHEN `costs of the proceeding generally` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- "and not the representative party" (ss 33Q(3), 33R(2)): a flat negative. For s 33Q(3) this assumes another
        -- person was appointed sub-group representative (fork F6).
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§§ `The representative party (ss 33T, 33W)`

-- s 33T(1) "If, on an application by a group member, it appears to the Court that a representative party is not able
-- adequately to represent the interests of the group members, the Court may substitute another group member"; (2) the
-- same for a sub-group. An "if": not so, no.
GIVEN `the Court finds the representative inadequate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33T -- the representative can be replaced on my application` `the Court finds the representative inadequate` MEANS
    IF `the Court finds the representative inadequate`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 33W(2) a representative party settling their own claim may, with leave, withdraw. (4) "Before granting a person
-- leave to withdraw ...: (a) the Court must be satisfied that notice of the application has been given to group members
-- in accordance with subsection 33X(1) and in sufficient time for them to apply to have another person substituted ...;
-- and (b) any application for the substitution ... has been determined." Both are preconditions: either unmet, no.
GIVEN `notice went to group members in time` IS A BOOLEAN, `every substitution application is determined` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33W(4) -- the representative can be let withdraw` `notice went to group members in time` `every substitution application is determined` MEANS
    IF `notice went to group members in time` AND `every substitution application is determined`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Stay, settlement and damages (ss 33U, 33V, 33X(4), 33Z(3))`

-- s 33U "Where a respondent ... commences a proceeding in the Court against a group member, the Court may order a stay of
-- execution in respect of any relief awarded to the group member ... until the other proceeding is determined."
GIVEN `the respondent is suing me in the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33U -- my award can be stayed` `the respondent is suing me in the Court` MEANS
    IF `the respondent is suing me in the Court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 33V(1) "A representative proceeding may not be settled or discontinued without the approval of the Court." s 33X(4)
-- "Unless the Court is satisfied that it is just to do so, an application for approval of a settlement under section 33V
-- must not be determined unless notice has been given to group members."
GIVEN `the Court approves` IS A BOOLEAN, `group members were given notice` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Court is satisfied it is just without notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 33V, 33X(4) -- the class action can be settled` `the Court approves` `group members were given notice` `the Court is satisfied it is just without notice` MEANS
    IF NOT `the Court approves`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `group members were given notice` OR `the Court is satisfied it is just without notice`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 33Z(1)(f) damages "in an aggregate amount without specifying amounts awarded in respect of individual group
-- members". (3) "Subject to section 33V, the Court is not to make an award of damages under paragraph (1)(f) unless a
-- reasonably accurate assessment can be made of the total amount". Under a settlement (s 33V) the bar is lifted and the
-- Act says no more. NOTHING-kind: silent (fork F7).
GIVEN `this is under a settlement` IS A BOOLEAN, `the total can be reasonably accurately assessed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33Z(3) -- damages can be awarded as a lump sum` `this is under a settlement` `the total can be reasonably accurately assessed` MEANS
    IF `this is under a settlement`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the total can be reasonably accurately assessed`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Division 3 -- notices (ss 33X, 33Y(8))`

DECLARE `What the notice is about` IS ONE OF
    `the start of the class action and my right to opt out`
    `the respondent's application to dismiss for want of prosecution`
    `the representative party's application to withdraw`
    `money paid into Court in answer to a claim`
    `an application to approve a settlement`
    `another matter`

-- s 33X(1) notice "must be given" of (a)-(c); (2) the Court may dispense with it "where the relief sought ... does not
-- include any claim for damages"; (3) "If the Court so orders", notice of money brought into Court; (4) settlement (see
-- above); (5) "The Court may, at any stage, order that notice of any matter be given"; (6) "as soon as practicable after
-- the happening of the event".
GIVEN m IS A `What the notice is about`, `damages are claimed` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Court dispensed with notice` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Court ordered notice` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Court is satisfied it is just without notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33X -- I must be given notice` m `damages are claimed` `the Court dispensed with notice` `the Court ordered notice` `the Court is satisfied it is just without notice` MEANS
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN `money paid into Court in answer to a claim` THEN
        IF `the Court ordered notice` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHEN `an application to approve a settlement` THEN
        -- s 33X(4) bars deciding the application without notice; it does not in terms require notice (fork F8).
        IF `the Court ordered notice` OR (NOT `the Court is satisfied it is just without notice`) THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHEN `another matter` THEN
        -- NOTHING-kind: silent (only s 33X(5) reaches other matters, and only by order).
        IF `the Court ordered notice` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the Court dispensed with notice` AND (NOT `damages are claimed`) AND (NOT `the Court ordered notice`)
        THEN JUST FALSE
        ELSE JUST TRUE

-- s 33Y(8) "The failure of a group member to receive or respond to a notice does not affect a step taken, an order made,
-- or a judgment given, in a proceeding." A flat negative.
`s 33Y(8) -- missing a notice affects the proceeding` MEANS JUST FALSE

§§ `Division 4 -- judgment and the fund (ss 33ZA, 33ZB, 33ZJ)`

-- s 33ZA(3)(c): the order constituting a fund must "specify a day (which is 6 months or more after the day on which the
-- order is made) on or before which the group members are to make a claim". The earliest day the order can name.
GIVEN `the day of the fund order` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 33ZA(3)(c) -- the earliest claim day` `the day of the fund order` MEANS
    `six months after` `the day of the fund order`

DECLARE `Fund party` IS ONE OF `the group member`
DECLARE `Fund action` IS ONE OF `make a claim for payment out of the fund`

-- s 33ZA(3)(c): group members "are to make a claim for payment out of the fund" on or before the claim day. A duty with
-- its own period, counted in days from the fund order; a claim on the claim day itself is in time.
GIVEN `days to the claim day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Fund party` `Fund action`
`s 33ZA(3)(c) -- I must claim by the claim day` `days to the claim day` MEANS
    PARTY `the group member`
    MUST `make a claim for payment out of the fund`
    WITHIN `days to the claim day`
    LEST BREACH BY `the group member` BECAUSE "claim after the s 33ZA(3)(c) claim day: only the Court can allow it, under s 33ZA(4)"

-- Runs the duty over when the claim was made. Takes no DEONTIC input and is not exported.
GIVEN `the day of the fund order` IS A DATE, `the claim day` IS A DATE, `the day I claim` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 33ZA(3)(c) -- my claim was in time` `the day of the fund order` `the claim day` `the day I claim` MEANS
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`s 33ZA(3)(c) -- I must claim by the claim day` (`days from` `the day of the fund order` `the claim day`)) 0 `the events`
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHERE
        `the events` MEANS
            LIST (EVENT `the group member` `make a claim for payment out of the fund` (`days from` `the day of the fund order` `the day I claim`)), (WAITUNTIL ((`days from` `the day of the fund order` `the day I claim`) PLUS (`days from` `the day of the fund order` `the claim day`) PLUS 2))

-- s 33ZA(4) "The Court may allow a group member to make a claim after the day fixed under paragraph (3)(c) if: (a) the
-- fund has not already been fully distributed; and (b) it is just to do so." An "if": either unmet, no.
GIVEN `the day of the fund order` IS A DATE, `the claim day` IS A DATE, `the day I claim` IS A DATE,
      `the fund is fully distributed` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Court thinks it just` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33ZA -- I can claim from the fund` `the day of the fund order` `the claim day` `the day I claim` `the fund is fully distributed` `the Court thinks it just` MEANS
    IF `s 33ZA(3)(c) -- my claim was in time` `the day of the fund order` `the claim day` `the day I claim`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF (NOT `the fund is fully distributed`) AND `the Court thinks it just`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 33ZB "A judgment ...: (a) must describe or otherwise identify the group members who will be affected by it; and (b)
-- binds all such persons other than any person who has opted out of the proceeding under section 33J." An opt-out:
-- "(other than X)" read as the text's no (fork F10). A person the judgment does not identify: NOTHING-kind: scope limit
-- (the section does not say such a person is not bound).
GIVEN `the judgment identifies me` IS A BOOLEAN, `I opted out` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33ZB -- the judgment binds me` `the judgment identifies me` `I opted out` MEANS
    IF `I opted out`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the judgment identifies me`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING

-- s 33ZJ(2) "If ... the Court is satisfied that the costs reasonably incurred ... by the person making the application
-- are likely to exceed the costs recoverable by the person from the respondent, the Court may order that an amount equal
-- to the whole or a part of the excess be paid to that person out of the damages awarded." (1) only "Where the Court has
-- made an award of damages". The most is the excess, and no more than the damages awarded (fork F11).
GIVEN `damages were awarded` IS A BOOLEAN, `the representative applied` IS A BOOLEAN, `costs reasonably incurred` IS A NUMBER,
      `costs recoverable from the respondent` IS A NUMBER, `damages awarded` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 33ZJ -- the most paid to the representative out of the damages` `damages were awarded` `the representative applied` `costs reasonably incurred` `costs recoverable from the respondent` `damages awarded` MEANS
    IF NOT (`damages were awarded` AND `the representative applied`)
    THEN JUST 0
    ELSE IF `costs reasonably incurred` AT MOST `costs recoverable from the respondent`
         THEN JUST 0
         ELSE IF (`costs reasonably incurred` MINUS `costs recoverable from the respondent`) AT LEAST `damages awarded`
              THEN JUST `damages awarded`
              ELSE JUST (`costs reasonably incurred` MINUS `costs recoverable from the respondent`)

§§ `Division 5 -- appeals (s 33ZC(6), with Federal Court Rules 2011 rr 1.61, 36.03)`

-- r 36.03: a notice of appeal must be filed "(a) within 28 days after: (i) the date on which the judgment appealed from was
-- pronounced or the order was made; or (ii) the date on which leave to appeal was granted; or (b) on or before a date
-- fixed for that purpose by the court appealed from." r 1.61(2): the day of the event is not counted; r 1.61(5): no day
-- from 24 December to 14 January is counted. Where the Court fixed a date, the later of the two is taken (fork F12).
-- Extensions of time (r 36.05) are not encoded.
GIVEN `the day time runs from` IS A DATE, `the Court fixed a date` IS A BOOLEAN, `the date fixed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`r 36.03 -- the representative's last day to appeal` `the day time runs from` `the Court fixed a date` `the date fixed` MEANS
    IF `the Court fixed a date`
    THEN `the later date of` (`the last day of n counted days after` `the day time runs from` 28) `the date fixed`
    ELSE `the last day of n counted days after` `the day time runs from` 28

-- s 33ZC(6) "If the representative party or the sub-group representative party does not bring an appeal within the time
-- provided for instituting appeals, another member of the group or sub-group may, within a further 21 days, bring an
-- appeal as representing the group members". The 21 days are fixed by the Act, not by the Rules or an order, so r 1.61(5)
-- does not take out the Christmas days (finding 4; fork F13).
GIVEN `the day time runs from` IS A DATE, `the Court fixed a date` IS A BOOLEAN, `the date fixed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 33ZC(6) -- my last day to appeal for the group` `the day time runs from` `the Court fixed a date` `the date fixed` MEANS
    `the day n days after` (`r 36.03 -- the representative's last day to appeal` `the day time runs from` `the Court fixed a date` `the date fixed`) 21

-- "If ... does not bring an appeal within the time": an "if" (JUST FALSE when the representative did appeal in time);
-- "within a further 21 days": the text's own period (ruling (a)), which starts only when the representative's time ends.
GIVEN `the day time runs from` IS A DATE, `the Court fixed a date` IS A BOOLEAN, `the date fixed` IS A DATE,
      `the representative appealed in time` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day I file` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33ZC(6) -- I can appeal for the group` `the day time runs from` `the Court fixed a date` `the date fixed` `the representative appealed in time` `the day I file` MEANS
    IF `the representative appealed in time`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF     `days from` (`r 36.03 -- the representative's last day to appeal` `the day time runs from` `the Court fixed a date` `the date fixed`) `the day I file` GREATER THAN 0
            AND `days from` `the day I file` (`s 33ZC(6) -- my last day to appeal for the group` `the day time runs from` `the Court fixed a date` `the date fixed`) AT LEAST 0
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Division 6 -- limitation periods and other laws (ss 33ZE, 33ZH)`

DECLARE `Where my claim stands` IS ONE OF
    `the class action is still going`
    `I opted out`
    `the class action and its appeals ended without finally disposing of my claim`
    `my claim was finally disposed of`

DECLARE `Limitation answer` IS ONE OF
    `my limitation period is suspended`
    `my limitation period runs again` HAS `my new last day` IS A DATE
    `my limitation period had already run out when the class action began`
    `section 33ZE does not reach my claim`
    `my claim was finally disposed of in the class action`

-- s 33ZE(1) "Upon the commencement of a representative proceeding, the running of any limitation period that applies to
-- the claim of a group member to which the proceeding relates is suspended." (2) "The limitation period does not begin to
-- run again unless either the member opts out ... under section 33J or the proceeding, and any appeals ..., are determined
-- without finally disposing of the group member's claim." The days left when the class action began are counted from the
-- day after it began to the old last day, and added to the day it runs again (fork F14).
GIVEN `my claim is in the class action` IS A BOOLEAN, `my old last day` IS A DATE, `the day the class action began` IS A DATE,
      s IS A `Where my claim stands`, `the day that happened` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Limitation answer`
`s 33ZE -- my limitation period` `my claim is in the class action` `my old last day` `the day the class action began` s `the day that happened` MEANS
    IF NOT `my claim is in the class action`
    THEN `section 33ZE does not reach my claim`
    ELSE IF `days from` `the day the class action began` `my old last day` LESS THAN 0
         THEN `my limitation period had already run out when the class action began`
         ELSE CONSIDER s
              WHEN `the class action is still going` THEN `my limitation period is suspended`
              WHEN `my claim was finally disposed of` THEN `my claim was finally disposed of in the class action`
              OTHERWISE `my limitation period runs again` (`the day n days after` `the day that happened` (`days from` `the day the class action began` `my old last day`))

-- s 33ZH(1) "a group member ... is to be taken to be a party to the proceeding" for s 87(1) of the Competition and
-- Consumer Act 2010 and s 238(1) of the Australian Consumer Law; (2) the representative party's application under
-- s 87(1A) or ACL s 237(1) "is to be taken to be an application by the representative party and all the group members".
GIVEN `I am a group member` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33ZH -- I count as a party for consumer law orders` `I am a group member` MEANS
    IF `I am a group member`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind: scope limit (the section speaks only of group members).
    ELSE NOTHING
